<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26425" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lēvītes</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lēvīta</span></b> , Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 2, 39; 5, 30), ae,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Levite</i>: Levita de tribu sacra, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 2, 39; 5, 30. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a deacon</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 9,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lē-vītĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Levi</i> or <i>to the Levites,
				Levitical</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus Leviticum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Deut. 17, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stirps,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ios. 3, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lēvītis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i>adj. f., of</i>
			or <i>belonging to the tribe of Levi</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gentis Levitidis una Semper fida comes,</span>”
				<i>of the Levites</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Psych. 502</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
